// Windows executable icon.
//
// Compiled INTO the binary by windres (MinGW) or rc.exe (MSVC). This is what
// Explorer, a desktop shortcut and a PINNED taskbar button read.
// QApplication::setWindowIcon() in main.cpp is a DIFFERENT mechanism that
// only dresses the windows the running process creates - neither substitutes
// for the other, so both are needed.
//
// The id matters: Windows shows the icon with the LOWEST resource id as the
// file's icon, so this stays 1.
//
// Forward slashes on purpose - windres and rc.exe both accept them, and a
// literal backslash here would have to be escaped.
//
// KEEP THIS FILE TRACKED. The stock Qt .gitignore in this directory carries a
// blanket `*.rc` rule, which is meant for the GENERATED resource scripts
// qmake used to emit (`*_resource.rc`, ignored on the line above it). This one
// is hand-written source. When it went untracked, a fresh clone had no
// app_icon.rc and CMake failed at CONFIGURE time with
//   Cannot find source file: .../app_icon.rc
// because qt_add_executable() names it. .gitignore now carries an explicit
// `!app_icon.rc` negation to stop that happening again.

1 ICON "assets/icons/ultracan_logo.ico"
